# 1. Ignore everything
**/*

# 2. Add files and directories that should be included
!apps/**
!libs/**
# The catalogs of every language the apps ship (i18n/TRANSLATING.md).
!i18n/**
!infra/**
!deno.jsonc
# The MPA renders the API reference and the published guides from these files
# (apps/mpa/api-docs.ts, PUBLISHED_DOCS in apps/mpa/docs-site.ts); the other docs stay out.
!docs/token-api.md
!docs/apps.md
!docs/products.md
!docs/start-a-product.md
!docs/deploy.md
!docs/guests.md
!docs/sign-in-providers.md
!docs/backups.md
!docs/files.md
!docs/data-export.md
!docs/capacity.md
!docs/billing.md
!docs/catalog.md
!docs/telegram.md
!docs/offline.md
!docs/security-headers.md
!docs/development.md
!docs/aggregates.md
!docs/ids.md
!docs/api-errors.md
!docs/admin-modules.md
# The website counts the browser test suites (apps/mpa/repo-facts.ts): the files at the top of
# e2e/, which holds only suites there, and none of its folders. Never write this as
# `!e2e/*.e2e.ts`: an exception with any wildcard but a trailing `/**` makes BuildKit read every
# folder of the context, and the server's `.volumes/` holds folders it may not open.
!e2e/**
e2e/*/**
!deno.lock

# 3. Bonus step: ignore any unnecessary files that may be inside those allowed directories in Step #2
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/node_modules
**/build
**/dist
**/Dockerfile
**/dockerfile
**/dockerfile.*
**/_fresh

# 4. Never let a secret into an image. On the server these folders hold the env file and the Web
#    Push key, and a developer may keep a .env beside an app; Compose hands the containers what they
#    need at run time (environment, a bind mount).
infra/envs
infra/configs
**/.env*
